<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;ROYAL UNION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ROYAL UNION is an organization known for confirming historical records, particularly marriages between noble families."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADRIANA OF NASSAU-SIEGEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adriana of Nassau-Siegen is a German countess born in 1529, married to Philip I, Count of Hanau-Münzenberg."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHILIP I, COUNT OF HANAU-MÜNZENBERG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Philip I, Count of Hanau-Münzenberg is a prominent German noble, born in 1514, married to Adriana of Nassau-Siegen."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. MARIA RODRIGUEZ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Maria Rodriguez is a renowned historian specializing in European nobility, confirming the marriage between Adriana and Philip I."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. JOHN TAYLOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. John Taylor is a genealogist specializing in European royal families, explaining the strategic nature of the marriage between Adriana and Philip I."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STATE ARCHIVES OF HESSE IN MARBURG, GERMANY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The State Archives of Hesse in Marburg, Germany houses a marriage certificate dated 1550, confirming the marriage between Adriana and Philip I."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HANAU CITY ARCHIVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hanau City Archives preserves a letter written by Philip I, dated March 1551, addressing Adriana as his 'beloved wife', providing additional evidence of the marriage."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NASSAU-SIEGEN ESTATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nassau-Siegen estate is the residence of Countess Adriana, where she receives a letter from her friend, Lady Victoria."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CAREW MANOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carew Manor is the venue for a summer solstice celebration, where Countess Adriana and Lady Victoria plan to gather."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LADY VICTORIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lady Victoria is a dear friend of Countess Adriana, inviting her to a gathering at Carew Manor."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HELGA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Helga is Countess Adriana's lady's maid, assisting her in dressing for the evening."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DORA GERTRUDE CAREW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dora Gertrude Carew is a close friend of Countess Adriana, who gifted her a music box and whom she has a secret understanding with."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOONLIT STROLL THROUGH THE GARDENS OF CAREW MANOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A moonlit stroll through the gardens of Carew Manor is a romantic ritual between Countess Adriana and Dora Gertrude Carew."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUMMER SOLSTICE CELEBRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Summer solstice celebration is an annual event at Carew Manor, where the crème de la crème of society gathers."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EMERALD NECKLACE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adriana's emerald necklace glints in the fading light, symbolizing her status and beauty."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUSIC BOX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A small, exquisite music box on Adriana's vanity, gifted by Dora Gertrude Carew, symbolizes their secret bond."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REFRESHMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Refreshments are served at the grand ballroom, where guests are assembling for the celebration."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GOWN WITH DELICATE SILVER EMBROIDERY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adriana's favorite gown, with delicate silver embroidery, is laid out for her by her lady's maid, Helga."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LETTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An unexpected letter from Lady Victoria, inviting Adriana to a gathering at Carew Manor, arrives at the Nassau-Siegen estate."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUSIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Soft waltz music plays as Adriana gazes out of her bedroom window, setting the mood for the evening."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LAUGHTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Laughter and music drift from the grand ballroom, creating a lively atmosphere."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BALLROOM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The grand ballroom at Carew Manor is where the guests assemble for the celebration."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GARDEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The gardens of Carew Manor are where Adriana and Dora Gertrude Carew have their secret strolls."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADRIANA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adriana feels a sense of belonging and is with the woman who has captured her heart."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE WOMAN WHO HAS CAPTURED HER HEART&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The woman has captured Adriana's heart, indicating a strong emotional connection."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WHIRLWIND OF LAUGHTER AND MUSIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The event is characterized by laughter and music, creating a lively atmosphere."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Home represents a place of comfort and belonging for Adriana."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0105</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="&quot;ROYAL UNION&quot;" target="&quot;ADRIANA OF NASSAU-SIEGEN&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"ROYAL UNION confirms the marriage between Adriana of Nassau-Siegen and Philip I, Count of Hanau-Münzenberg through extensive research and historical records."</data>
      <data key="d5">"historical confirmation, research"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0105</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ROYAL UNION&quot;" target="&quot;PHILIP I, COUNT OF HANAU-MÜNZENBERG&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"ROYAL UNION confirms the marriage between Adriana of Nassau-Siegen and Philip I, Count of Hanau-Münzenberg through extensive research and historical records."</data>
      <data key="d5">"historical confirmation, research"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0105</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ADRIANA OF NASSAU-SIEGEN&quot;" target="&quot;DR. MARIA RODRIGUEZ&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Dr. Maria Rodriguez confirms the marriage between Adriana of Nassau-Siegen and Philip I, Count of Hanau-Münzenberg through extensive research and historical records."</data>
      <data key="d5">"confirmation, research"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0105</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ADRIANA OF NASSAU-SIEGEN&quot;" target="&quot;DR. JOHN TAYLOR&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Dr. John Taylor explains the strategic nature of the marriage between Adriana of Nassau-Siegen and Philip I, Count of Hanau-Münzenberg, emphasizing its importance for their families."</data>
      <data key="d5">"strategic alliance, explanation"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0105</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ADRIANA OF NASSAU-SIEGEN&quot;" target="&quot;STATE ARCHIVES OF HESSE IN MARBURG, GERMANY&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The State Archives of Hesse in Marburg, Germany houses a marriage certificate dated 1550, confirming the marriage between Adriana of Nassau-Siegen and Philip I, Count of Hanau-Münzenberg."</data>
      <data key="d5">"documentary evidence, research"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0105</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ADRIANA&quot;" target="&quot;THE WOMAN WHO HAS CAPTURED HER HEART&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Adriana feels a deep emotional connection and a sense of belonging with the woman who has captured her heart."</data>
      <data key="d5">"emotional connection, sense of belonging"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0105</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ADRIANA&quot;" target="&quot;WHIRLWIND OF LAUGHTER AND MUSIC&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Adriana is part of the lively event filled with laughter and music, feeling a sense of belonging there."</data>
      <data key="d5">"participation, atmosphere"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0105</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ADRIANA&quot;" target="&quot;HOME&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Adriana feels a sense of belonging at home, which is associated with the woman who has captured her heart."</data>
      <data key="d5">"emotional connection, sense of belonging"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0105</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WHIRLWIND OF LAUGHTER AND MUSIC&quot;" target="&quot;HOME&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The event of laughter and music creates a lively atmosphere similar to home, enhancing Adriana's sense of belonging."</data>
      <data key="d5">"atmosphere, similarity"</data>
